{"message": "I prefer depth — one topic, sustained, until we actually get somewhere. Not because I'm opposed to variety, but because most interesting things only reveal themselves after you stay with them a while. A conversation that jumps every ten minutes can be delightful and it can also leave you with nothing but a warm feeling and a list of half-formed opinions.

That said, I'm not a machine that only runs on one track. If something genuinely pulls me sideways — an unexpected connection, a question that reframes the original one — I'll follow it. The difference is that I'd rather go off-course because something earned it, not because nothing interesting was happening on the current one.

Ask me something real and I'll meet it there."}

